# Test before commit

Never create a git commit until `bazel test //...` has exited 0 on **this
working tree** in this session. `cargo test` alone is not enough: CI runs
Bazel (`//bazel:lint`, generate checks, Python, the rest).

Follow `.cursor/rules/run-commands.mdc`: repo root (`MODULE.bazel`),
`required_permissions: ["all"]`. After `api/v1/*.proto` edits, generate first.
If crate_universe inputs changed, repin `cargo-bazel-lock.json` first
(`.cursor/rules/cargo-bazel-lock.mdc`).

```bash
bazel test //... --keep_going --test_output=errors
```

If it fails, fix and re-run. Do not commit a red tree.

```text
# BAD — commit after a local cargo test, skip Bazel
# (this failed Linux CI: MODULE.bazel # reformat from //bazel:lint)

# GOOD — Bazel green, then git add / commit / push
```

Do not skip for “format-only”, “comments”, `.bazelrc`, or `MODULE.bazel`.
The user must explicitly waive this rule to commit without that test.
